    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0794" n="785" xml:id="pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">617.003/242: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-12T19:00:00-05:00">January 12, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Your telegram No. 3, January 10, 6 p.m. You should inform the Nicaraguan
                    Foreign Minister<anchor n="4" xml:id="d727-f1"/> that the proposed increase in
                    the rate of exchange for the payment of import duties which would require that
                    import duties prescribed in Schedule I of the trade agreement be paid in
                    cordobas at the official rate of exchange for the United States dollar involves
                    the important question of the effect of the proposed measure upon the trade
                    agreement. The Department hopes that action in regard to the measure will be
                    deferred until the views of this Government with respect thereto can be
                    communicated to the Nicaraguan Government. The Department hopes to be able to
                    transmit such views within a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
